// INHERITED COMPILER DEFECT, characterised 2026-09-14 (ROADMAP A27). Five lines.
//   ./seed/build/seed ./bebop.bin compile <this> out.bin   ->  rc=201
//   0:0: error[E201]: compiler self-check 7.1
// The self-check is bebop.bp:5760: at a statement boundary the window is EMPTY
// (fntab[5387] == 0) while the callee-saved mask (fntab[5389]) still has non-hoist
// bits set -- a cs register marked live with nothing on the window.
// ISOLATED, not inferred. `*=` is the ONLY compound assignment that does it:
// += -= /= %= all give rc=0 on the identical program. The RHS must be a `let ... in`
// whose binding contains a CALL (builtin or user -- clz and a user fn both do it);
// `let t1 = 0 in 17` gives rc=0. No second function, no loop, no match, no recursion
// and no enum are needed -- an earlier 18-line version carried all of them.
// PRE-A18: the pre-A18 compiler 072c01d1 gives the identical message, so this is NOT
// caused by `return`/`break` in expression position, which it was first blamed on.
fn main() -> i64 {
  let v0 = 1;
  v0 *= (let t1 = clz(1) in 17);
  v0
}
